  "configuration_id": "config_045",
  "reason": "All four completed experiments are singleprofile, so we have zero evidence on whether multiprofile + aggregation improves performance. The best result so far is config_038 (multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l, weighted fusion, acc=0.537). config_045 is the minimal, controlled extension of that best result: it keeps the same model setting, RNA encoder, image encoder, and fusion method, and only changes profile_setting from single to multi with avgpool aggregation (which is inherent to multiprofile). This directly tests whether representing each cell with multiple profiles and aggregating them (vs. a single profile) yields a meaningful gain. If multiprofile helps, it opens a large and promising sub-space; if it does not, we can confidently prune all multiprofile configurations and focus remaining budget on RNA/image encoder and fusion refinements within singleprofile. Under a tight budget, resolving this high-impact binary question with a one-axis change from our current best is the most information-efficient next step."
}

